      "solution": "chomp(my $tour = <STDIN>);\n\nmy @cube=(0,1,3,2,4,5,7,6);\nmy @length=(0,1,sqrt 2,sqrt 5);\nmy $length=0;\nmy $from;\n\nfor my $to (map{$cube[$_-1]} split(//,$tour)) {\n    $length += $length[unpack('%32b*',pack('C',$from^$to))] if(defined $from);\n    $from = $to;\n}\n\nprintf(\"%.3f\\n\",$length);",
      "statement": "You are an ant on a solid regular cube with a side length of 1. You can walk freely on the cube's surface.\n\nYou are given a tour of [[n]] corner numbers. You start at the first corner of the tour and visit all remaining corners of the tour in the tour's sequence. The tour stops at the last tour corner. A tour may or may not start and end at the same corner. A tour can also visit the same corners multiple times.\n\nThe cube's corners are numbered as depicted here:\n```\n   8----------7\n  /|         /|\n / |        / |\n4----------3  |\n|  |       |  |\n|  5-------|--6\n| /        | /\n|/         |/\n1----------2\n```\nOr if you prefer an image:  https://postimg.cc/PpNvDXjt\n\nFind and output the shortest total length of the tour. The length has to be rounded to 3 decimal digits.",
